WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.800
Unit 2 is the reader.

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.494
Google's Event resource has
the one category, a state,

3
00:00:05.494 --> 00:00:09.188
a detailed category, relevance,
impacts and updates.

4
00:00:09.188 --> 00:00:12.226
Here's what Google leaves to
you, and what the kit adds.

5
00:00:12.226 --> 00:00:16.059
With one category, every
Google notice is an incident,

6
00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:21.200
and the gap is written down in the guide,
the chapter and the ISSO's record.

7
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.306
Impacts come as product
and location objects;

8
00:00:24.306 --> 00:00:27.413
they become the record's
services and regions.

9
00:00:27.413 --> 00:00:29.892
An event's description is sometimes empty,

10
00:00:29.892 --> 00:00:32.725
so the kit takes the latest
update's description.

11
00:00:32.725 --> 00:00:35.612
There's no field that
says action is required,

12
00:00:35.612 --> 00:00:39.670
and the kit adds no action rule
for Google: an open incident that

13
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:43.650
names resources routes by the
agency's own routing, in Module 7.

14
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:47.945
Google's A P I returns a response
object and G cloud a bare list,

15
00:00:47.945 --> 00:00:49.663
and the kit accepts both.

16
00:00:49.663 --> 00:00:51.699
A closed state closes the record,

17
00:00:51.699 --> 00:00:56.450
and the detailed category and relevance
are kept as the provider's severity.

18
00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.197
The kit has no separate
government endpoint for

19
00:00:59.197 --> 00:01:02.060
Personalized Service
Health; the cloud is global.
